    "body": "Relay BB run pushed an update.\n\nPull request: #336\n\nTokens: 0 · Cost: $0.0000\n\nPushed successfully to branch `bb/relay-130-approval-baseline-01-03-create-pending-thr_bi593223wx`.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplements issue #130: creates pending approval requests synchronously in the outbound MCP-invoke choke point.\n\n- Added migration `0021_approval_requests.sql` creating the `approval_requests` table (uuid id, `agent_run_id` FK, `tool_name`, `risk_class` snapshot, `payload` jsonb snapshot of the deferred invocation, `status` pending/approved/rejected, `requested_at`, `decided_at`, nullable `decided_by` FK to `users`).\n- Added `backend/packages/data/src/mcp/approvalRequestsStore.ts` with `createPendingApprovalRequest` / `getApprovalRequest`, exported from the package's public surface.\n- Added `createApprovalGatedMcpInvokeTool` in `backend/packages/agent-runtime/src/mcpInvokeTool.ts`: resolves and validates a call exactly like the existing `createMcpInvokeTool`, but when the resolved target requires approval, transactionally inserts one pending request (snapshotting tool name, risk class, and the exact deferred invocation) instead of executing the call, and returns a synthetic success result carrying the request id — so the turn/run completes normally as `done`. Non-approval tools continue straight through to execution.\n- Added test coverage for the store and for both the deferred and pass-through invocation paths.\n\nVerified: full monorepo build, unit suite (83/83), integration suite (618/618), e2e suite (5/5), lint, dependency-boundary check, and migration-ordinal check all pass.\n\nRelay-Step-Status: pass",
